apple-ib-tb: restore the Touch Bar on plain resume, not only reset_resume

appletb_suspend() turns the Touch Bar's mode and display off. The driver only
restores them in .reset_resume, which runs when USB resets the device (S3).
After s2idle the device resumes without a reset, the HID core calls .resume,
which is unset, so the Touch Bar stays dark until the module is reloaded.
Use the same restore function for .resume.

--- a/apple-ib-tb.c
+++ b/apple-ib-tb.c
@@ -1231,6 +1231,7 @@
 	.input_configured = appletb_input_configured,
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
 	.suspend = appletb_suspend,
+	.resume = appletb_reset_resume,
 	.reset_resume = appletb_reset_resume,
 #endif
 };
